WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.050
1. Turn the bike over, open the quick release and drop the wheel out

00:00:11.050 --> 00:00:29.816
2. Take the skewer out: nut off, slide it out, springs narrow end in

00:00:29.816 --> 00:00:47.516
3. Spin the wheel and run your fingers round the braking track

00:00:47.516 --> 00:00:56.216
4. Check the brake calipers and pads from above

00:00:56.216 --> 00:01:20.916
5. Set the wheel back in the fork with the tread arrow pointing forward, then check the rear tire the same way

00:01:20.916 --> 00:01:45.082
6. Slide the skewer back through the hub and thread the nut on

00:01:45.082 --> 00:02:11.882
7. Snug the nut and close the lever flat along the fork

00:02:11.882 --> 00:02:26.798
8. Spin the wheel and squeeze the brake

